---
// Illustrated project page for the Bird Species Identification bachelor's
// thesis, ported from design-reference/bird-explainer.html. Replaces the page
// generated from src/content/projects/bird-species-identification.md (see
// explainers.ts). The reference's "Read the thesis" button is left out: the
// thesis PDF isn't public.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BirdSpeciesExplainer from '../../components/projects/BirdSpeciesExplainer.astro';
import '../../components/projects/explainer.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Bird Species Identification"
  description="A transfer-learning image classifier that names a bird's species from a single photo — VGG-16 and ResNet-18 fine-tuned on a 20-species slice of CUB-200-2011, explained stage by stage. Bachelor's thesis, 2021."
  type="article"
>
  <article class="wrap view xp">
    <nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/projects/">Projects</a> <span aria-hidden="true">›</span> <span aria-current="page">Bird Species Identification</span>
    </nav>
    <ul class="chips">
      <li class="chip">Bachelor's thesis · 2021</li>
      <li class="chip">Transfer learning</li>
      <li class="chip">VGG-16 · ResNet-18</li>
      <li class="chip">PyTorch</li>
    </ul>
    <h1 class="title">Bird Species Identification</h1>
    <p class="plain">Even expert birders disagree on a species from one photo. Can a network learn to tell them apart from only a handful of examples each?</p>
    <p class="meta">A transfer-learning image classifier that names a bird's species from a single photo — standing on the shoulders of networks already trained on millions of images, then re-taught on a small bird dataset.</p>
    <ul class="badges">
      <li class="badge"><span class="n">20</span><span class="l">Bird species (CUB-200 subset)</span></li>
      <li class="badge"><span class="n">743</span><span class="l">Training images · ~37 each</span></li>
      <li class="badge"><span class="n">2</span><span class="l">Backbones compared</span></li>
    </ul>

    <BirdSpeciesExplainer />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
